  "coverage": "All India, all industries (NIC 99999); every indicator the ASI 2008 block publishes — the complete factory accounts, 56 of 57 served with data",
  "note": "Monetary series are as published in the source: ₹ lakh (1 lakh = 100,000; 1 crore = 100 lakh). Count series (factories, persons) are plain counts. Survey years are fiscal (Apr–Mar), plotted at April of the first year. Nothing is selected or derived here: every published indicator, keyed i01–i57 in the source's own order, units as served (₹ lakh for money, counts and mandays plain, kWh and tonnes where marked). Stock-change indicators (24–27) and Net Profit (30) can be legitimately negative. Two source defects are handled and disclosed: the 2023-24 4-digit copies of indicators 36–49 arrive shifted one indicator down and are outvoted by the clean 2- and 3-digit copies; indicator 36 (children workers) exists ONLY as one such corrupt row and is quarantined — 56 of 57 indicators are baked.",
  "gaps": []
 },
